  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1246 PM MDT Thu Aug 6 2026\n\nDaytime temperatures will warm by 5 or more degrees over yesterday's \nhighs as the ridge axis shifts directly overhead. A HEAT ADVISORY \nhas been issued for the South Hills, Raft River Region, and the \nFranklin/Eastern Oneida region from 1 PM Friday through 11 PM \nSaturday. Widespread temperatures of 95 to 100 degrees are \nanticipated across the advised areas with overnight lows only \ndropping into the upper-60s. Outside of these areas, temperatures \nwill still warm into the upper-90s and even triple digits across the \neastern Magic Valley, but overnight temperatures will provide a tad \nmore relief as lows will manage to drop into the lower 60s. \nAdditionally, a limiting factor to the forecast warmth will be the \nsmoke and how much it limits our daytime heating. Models show near-\nsurface smoke increasing Friday, especially across the eastern Magic \nValley and areas further north. Temperatures on Saturday will run \nfairly similar, although both daytime and overnight temperatures \nwill likely cool by a few degrees as the ridge of high pressure is \nvery slightly flattened. As for winds, afternoon gusts today will \nreach around 20 to 25 mph and will increase heading further into the \nweekend, with gusts reaching 25 to 30 mph in more areas. Heading \ninto early next week, a Pacific trough along the CA coast will open \nthe door for monsoon moisture to lift northward by middle of next \nweek.",
